      "title": "Research Development Manager – Research Projects",
      "description": "Research Development Manager – Research Projects | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Skip to main content Bond University Study Contact us en English Afrikaans (Afrikaans) Arabic (العربية) Azerbaijani (Azərbaycan) Bengali (বাংলা) Catalan (Català) Chinese Simplified (简体中文) Chinese Traditional (繁體中文) Croatian (Hrvatski) Czech (čeština) Danish (Dansk) Dutch (Nederlands) Filipino (Tagalog) Finnish (Suomi) French (Français) Georgian (ქართული) German (Deutsch) Greek (Ελληνικά) Gujarati (ગુજરાતી) Hebrew (עברית) Hindi (हिन्दी) Hungarian (Magyar) Indonesian (Bahasa Indonesia) Irish (Gaeilge) Italian (Italiano) Japanese (日本語) Khmer (ខ្មែរ) Korean (한국어) Kurdish - Kurmanji (Kurmancî) Kurdish - Sorani (سۆرانی) Lao (ລາວ) Malay (Bahasa Melayu) Malayalam (മലയാളം) Mongolian (Монгол) Nepali (नेपाली) Norwegian (Norsk) Pashto (پښتو) Persian (فارسی) Polish (Polski) Portuguese (Português) Punjabi (ਪੰਜਾਬੀ) Romanian (Română) Russian (Русский) Samoan (Gagana Sāmoa) Serbian (Српски) Slovak (slovenčina) Slovenian (Slovenščina) Spanish (Español) Swahili (Kiswahili) Swedish (Svenska) Tamil (தமிழ்) Thai (ไทย) Turkish (Türkçe) Ukrainian (Українська) Urdu (اردو) Vietnamese (Tiếng Việt) Welsh (Cymraeg) Search Menu Bond University Study Contact us Search Close Loading main navigation We're sorry, an error occurred loading the main menu, please try again later. Bond University Study Contact us Close Menu Search Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Research Development Manager – Research Projects Start of main\n      content. Research Development Manager – Research Projects Full-time, Fixed Term for 12 months Reference number: 184678144 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Support high-quality health and medical research by helping researchers plan, establish and manage research projects. Work closely with academic staff, Faculty leadership and central University teams to strengthen research capability and delivery. Contribute to effective research administration, financial oversight and reporting in a collaborative Faculty environment. Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# The Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine is seeking a Research Development Manager – Research Projects with strong research administration experience and a practical understanding of the end-to-end research project lifecycle in a higher education or Australian research sector environment. Reporting to the Faculty Business Director, the position works closely with academic staff, the Associate Dean Research, Faculty leadership and central University teams to support research projects from early feasibility and funding development through to establishment, financial management, governance, reporting and delivery. The position will: Support Faculty researchers to effectively manage their projects throughout the research project lifecycle, from funding opportunity review, proposal development and project establishment through to ethics, contracts, reporting and close-out requirements. Provide practical research administration advice across funding rules, governance obligations, compliance requirements, budgets and deliverables. Work with academic investigators, ORS, Finance, HR, Legal, Research Ethics and external partners to keep research projects coordinated, compliant and on track. Contribute to research reporting, funding opportunity mapping, project monitoring and continuous improvement in Faculty research administration. About the person The successful candidate will bring hands-on research administration experience, ideally gained in a university, medical research institute, hospital research office or Australian research funding environment. This role will suit someone who understands how funded research projects move from idea to application, approval, establishment and delivery, and who can provide clear, practical support to researchers at each stage. Brings solid research administration experience and a practical understanding of the end-to-end research project lifecycle, from pre-award planning through to project set-up, governance, reporting and close-out. Is proactive and organised, with the ability to keep timelines, budgets, milestones and competing priorities moving without losing sight of the detail. Works collaboratively across academic and professional teams, building trust with researchers, central University teams and external partners. Communicates clearly and confidently, turning funding, compliance and project requirements into practical advice that helps researchers progress their work. Salary details The salary for the position commences at $99,108 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Please note: The fixed term of this employment contract will be for an initial 12 months. The prospect of extension will be discussed at the end of the contract term. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Fiona Rogers, Faculty Business Director on frogers@bond.edu.au Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Wednesday 23 September 2026 Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 23rd September 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072 This website uses cookies and other tracking technologies to enhance user experience and to analyse performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Manage preferences Reject all Accept cookies Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Data When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalised web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more an