      "title": "HSM Compliance Officer",
      "description": "HSM Compliance Officer | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Skip to main content Bond University Study Contact us en English Afrikaans (Afrikaans) Arabic (العربية) Azerbaijani (Azərbaycan) Bengali (বাংলা) Catalan (Català) Chinese Simplified (简体中文) Chinese Traditional (繁體中文) Croatian (Hrvatski) Czech (čeština) Danish (Dansk) Dutch (Nederlands) Filipino (Tagalog) Finnish (Suomi) French (Français) Georgian (ქართული) German (Deutsch) Greek (Ελληνικά) Gujarati (ગુજરાતી) Hebrew (עברית) Hindi (हिन्दी) Hungarian (Magyar) Indonesian (Bahasa Indonesia) Irish (Gaeilge) Italian (Italiano) Japanese (日本語) Khmer (ខ្មែរ) Korean (한국어) Kurdish - Kurmanji (Kurmancî) Kurdish - Sorani (سۆرانی) Lao (ລາວ) Malay (Bahasa Melayu) Malayalam (മലയാളം) Mongolian (Монгол) Nepali (नेपाली) Norwegian (Norsk) Pashto (پښتو) Persian (فارسی) Polish (Polski) Portuguese (Português) Punjabi (ਪੰਜਾਬੀ) Romanian (Română) Russian (Русский) Samoan (Gagana Sāmoa) Serbian (Српски) Slovak (slovenčina) Slovenian (Slovenščina) Spanish (Español) Swahili (Kiswahili) Swedish (Svenska) Tamil (தமிழ்) Thai (ไทย) Turkish (Türkçe) Ukrainian (Українська) Urdu (اردو) Vietnamese (Tiếng Việt) Welsh (Cymraeg) Search Menu Bond University Study Contact us Search Close Loading main navigation We're sorry, an error occurred loading the main menu, please try again later. Bond University Study Contact us Close Menu Search Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond HSM Compliance Officer Start of main\n      content. HSM Compliance Officer Full-time, Two-Year Fixed Term Appointment Reference number: 167864256 About the position As Australia's first private University, Bond University based at Robina, Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Showcase your strong organisational and administrative skills Join a supportive, and collaborative team environment Enjoy excellent staff benefits in a central Robina location HSM Compliance Officer Faculty of Health Sciences and Medicine Join Australia’s number one University for teaching*, and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# This is a fantastic opportunity to join a dynamic, supportive, and collaborative team with a strong emphasis on wellbeing, and with opportunities for professional development, variety, flexibility, and the chance to make a difference in shaping the future! Join the Faculty of Health Sciences & Medicine in a pivotal role supporting students as they prepare for professional placements. Reporting to the Senior Manager, Student Affairs & Service Quality, the HSM Compliance Officer is responsible for managing and overseeing student compliance with regulatory, accreditation, and university requirements, ensuring students are placement-ready and supported throughout their programs. The main responsibilities for this role include: Acting as the primary contact for students, staff, and external partners regarding compliance matters. Monitoring, assessing, and reporting on student compliance using established policies and procedures. Receiving, triaging, and escalating compliance issues where required. Maintaining accurate and confidential compliance records, documentation, and databases. Using software systems to produce reports, support quality assurance, and provide training to staff and students. Working collaboratively with placement teams to ensure smooth processes that support student success. This role would suit someone who enjoys working independently, thrives in a fast-paced environment, and is motivated by making a meaningful contribution to positive student outcomes. About the person We are seeking a proactive, detail-focused professional who can manage complex compliance requirements with confidence while building positive working relationships across the Faculty. The ideal candidate will demonstrate: Relevant qualification in health sciences, health administration, or a related field, or equivalent experience in health professional compliance, clinical coordination, or student placement administration within healthcare or higher education settings. Demonstrated ability to interpret and apply regulatory frameworks, professional standards, and institutional policies to ensure compliance and quality assurance. Proven experience managing fitness-to-practice or similar risk-based processes, including investigating concerns, triaging matters, and mitigating risk while maintaining confidentiality and sound judgement. Strong administrative and governance capability, with excellent organisational skills and a high level of accuracy in managing sensitive and confidential information. Advanced digital proficiency, including strong Microsoft Office skills and experience using university or health-sector systems (such as student placement platforms) to support compliance and operational efficiency. Experience rapidly learning and implementing new systems and technologies, including training and supporting staff to ensure effective adoption. Ability to work independently in a high-volume environment while contributing positively to team outcomes and continuous improvement. Salary details The salary for the position will commence at $90,587.42 plus 12% superannuation per annum. Additional information Enquiries regarding this appointment can be directed to Ms Audrey Chung, at achung@bond.edu.au or 07 5595 1269. Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria. Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59 PM, Sunday 27 th September 2026. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity.  In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at any time during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 27th September 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072 This website uses cookies and other tracking technologies to enhance user experience and to analyse performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Manage preferences Reject all Accept cookies Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Data When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give 