    "https://bond.edu.au/jobs/11132/office-and-events-coordinator": {
      "title": "Office and Events Coordinator",
      "description": "Office and Events Coordinator | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Skip to main content Bond University Study Contact us Search Menu Bond University Study Contact us Search Close Loading main navigation We're sorry, an error occurred loading the main menu, please try again later. Bond University Study Contact us Close Menu Oops, something went wrong. Load search widget Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Office and Events Coordinator Start of main\n      content. Office and Events Coordinator Full-time, Fixed Term for 2 years Reference number: 184680261 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina and Brisbane seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Play a key role in the growth and success of Bond Brisbane A varied, hands-on role spanning events, people, administration and client experience. Work independently, take ownership and build strong relationships across Bond and with external partner Office and Events Coordinator Bond Brisbane, Executive Learning Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: 36.75 hour standard work week Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents Corporate health and finance discounts Bond University’s is looking for a highly organised, proactive and personable Office & Events Coordinator to join our team at Bond Brisbane. This is a varied and hands-on role that sits at the heart of the day-to-day operation of our Brisbane campus. You will help support the delivery of executive education programs, corporate events and University activities, while ensuring our clients, learners, presenters and visitors receive an exceptional experience every time they engage with Bond Brisbane. No two days will be the same. One day you might be coordinating a corporate event, organising catering and room layouts; the next you could be supporting an executive education program, responding to client enquiries, assisting with financial administration or helping develop content to promote an upcoming event. About the person You will be an organised and adaptable professional who enjoys working in a varied role with busy periods around events and program delivery. You will be comfortable moving between administration, event coordination, customer service and practical operational tasks, including setting up and packing down rooms, setting and clearing tables, washing dishes, managing refreshments and supplies, and ensuring the venue is clean, tidy and ready for the next event. The role will require evening work to support programs, events and stakeholder engagement. You will bring: A degree and/or 3–5 years' relevant experience in events, corporate learning, administration, organisational development or a related field. Excellent organisational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities. Self-motivated and able to work independently, take initiative and manage tasks with minimal supervision. Strong interpersonal and communication skills and a genuine customer-service mindset. Confidence working with a wide range of stakeholders, including senior executives, clients, academics, facilitators, learners and external partners. Strong computer skills, particularly Microsoft Office and event management systems. Initiative, sound judgement and the ability to resolve issues professionally and independently. A willingness to get involved and take a hands-on approach when required – from coordinating an event to setting up a room and ensuring the venue is ready for guests. The ability to work collaboratively in a small team and across different areas of the University. Experience in higher education, executive education, corporate learning or events will be highly regarded. Salary details The salary for this full-time position is $88,111.17, per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Please note: The fixed term of this employment contract will be for up to two years, with twelve months' probation. The prospect of conversion to a continuing employment contract will be discussed at the end of the contract term. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Tim Burton, Director of Executive Learning email [email protected] ,au Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Friday 18th September 2026 Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 18th September 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
