    "https://bond.edu.au/jobs/11210/service-support-administrator": {
      "title": "About the position",
      "description": "Service Support Administrator | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Skip to main content Bond University Study Contact us Search Menu Bond University Study Contact us Search Close Loading main navigation We're sorry, an error occurred loading the main menu, please try again later. Bond University Study Contact us Close Menu Oops, something went wrong. Load search widget Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Service Support Administrator Start of main\n      content. Service Support Administrator Full-time, Continuing Reference number: 201396163 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Build your technical expertise and be the go-to expert for a wide range of IT systems and tools at Bond. Work in an environment that values continuous learning and career success. Work alongside passionate professionals who value teamwork and collaboration. Service Support Administrator Information Technology Services Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# The Service Support Administrator is responsible for the administration, support, security, and lifecycle management of the University's end-user computing environment. The role manages endpoint technologies including Microsoft Intune, Microsoft Defender for Endpoint, Windows Autopilot, operating system deployment, software deployment, and endpoint security solutions, ensuring secure, reliable, and efficient services for staff and students. The position also provides advanced technical support, develops and maintains standard operating environments (SOEs), automates operational processes, and contributes technical expertise to projects and service improvements. About the person To be successful in the Service Support Administrator role, candidates should demonstrate the following qualifications, skills, and experience: Relevant qualifications and experience : Degree in Information Technology, or an equivalent combination of industry certifications, technical training, and practical experience in endpoint management and support. Endpoint management expertise : Advanced knowledge and hands-on experience with Microsoft Intune, Windows Autopilot, operating system deployment, software deployment, configuration management, and endpoint administration. Endpoint security knowledge : Strong experience with Microsoft Defender for Endpoint, endpoint security technologies, anti-malware, application control, security baselines, attack surface reduction, and least-privilege access management. Technical troubleshooting and automation skills : Demonstrated ability to diagnose and resolve complex endpoint issues, supported by strong knowledge of Windows networking (DNS, DHCP) and experience developing and deploying PowerShell scripts and automation solutions. Customer service and communication skills : Proven ability to provide professional customer-focused support, manage escalated technical issues, communicate effectively with stakeholders, and work collaboratively across technical and business teams. Desirable experience : Experience in a higher education environment, relevant Microsoft certifications, and knowledge of additional endpoint platforms such as macOS, Jamf, iPadOS, and Android. Salary details The salary for the position commences at $99,108.89 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Nathan Maguire, Manager End Device Services, [email protected] +61 7 5595 3529 Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above Given the expected large volume of applications, priority will be given to those applicants who clearly present examples against the Selection Criteria using the STAR method (Situation, Task, Action, Result). For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Sunday 4 th October 2026 Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 4th October 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    },
    "https://bond.edu.au/jobs/11209/future-student-advisor": {
      "title": "About the position",
      "description": "Future Student Advisor | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Skip to main content Bond University Study Contact us Search Menu Bond University Study Contact us Search Close Loading main navigation We're sorry, an error occurred loading the main menu, please try again later. Bond University Study Contact us Close Menu Oops, something went wrong. Load search widget Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Future Student Advisor Start of main\n      content. Future Student Advisor Full time, Fixed Term Appointment for 2 Years Reference number: 201395598 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Excellent location and benefits package Join a premium brand and support student recruitment Varied role that encompasses sales, relationship building and expertise in study options Future Student Advisor Office of Future Students Full time, Fixed Term Appointment for 2 Years Position Reference No: 201395598 Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# About the Position Future Student Advisors engage with prospective domestic and international students and their families with enquiries about study options at Bond University across multiple channels, including walk-in, telephone and digital channels. As the first contact point for prospective students, you will be expected to resolve a variety of questions along with using a consultative sales approach to troubleshoot enquiries in the broad fields of recruitment and sales, relationship management, study options at Bond and program application assistance. Reporting to the Team Lead, the position of Future Student Advisor will assist in driving student recruitment for the University with a strong focus on consistently delivering premium experiences to increase conversion percentage. About the person We are seeking a motivated team player who truly cares about achieving the best outcomes for our future students. You will be an exceptional and confident communicator and have the ability and passion to accurately articulate the value of the Bond University Brand. Other skills include: Demonstrated ability to work under pressure, maintain attention to detail in a fast-paced environment, display sound judgement, and to use initiative. Excellent time management and organisational skills, with ability to prioritise workloads to ensure deadlines are met. Experience working with international and domestic students Highly developed customer service skills with an innovative approach to go the extra mile and achieve targets. Outstanding business and analysis skills. A high level of accuracy and attention to detail A bachelor’s degree in a relevant discipline or equivalent experience will be ideal. Additionally working for a premium brand, higher education product knowledge is desirable. Salary details The salary for this position commences at $85,707.07 plus 12% superannuation per annum. Please note: The fixed term of this employment contract will be for up to two years, with twelve months' probation. The prospect of conversion to a continuing employment contract will be discussed at the end of the contract term. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Dee Littlewood, Team Lead, Application Success (Offshore) at [email protected] . Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Monday, 5 October 2026. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 Applications close: 5th October 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
    },
