 Medical and health services Student counselling Accessibility and inclusion Accessibility resources Feedback and questions University security Escape | Hide | Tell Emergency contacts Career Development Centre About the Career Development Centre Careers information for all our current students Employers and Industry Global experiences Graduates and alumni Verification of qualifications What's On Preventing and responding to gender-based violence Wellbeing services Student Wellbeing Advisors JP/Commissioner for Declarations service LGBTIQ+ services and support Campus life Bond University Student Association Student clubs Faculty Student Associations Bond University Business Students' Association Health and Sport Sciences Student Association (HSA) Medical Students Society of Bond University (MSSBU) Law Student Association Society & Design Student Association Club events Student events Students living on campus Sports Centre Smoke-free campus Merchandise Store Student Services and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Application procedure Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Study Why study at Bond Career ready Career development support Start of main\n      content. Career development support Empowering career-ready graduates It’s not always easy working out what you want to do, and how you want to do it. Here at Bond, the transition from university to employment starts from your earliest days on campus. From Orientation to graduation, we encourage you to engage with the Career Development Centre, pursue opportunities to develop your employability, and learn about the full range of support services that will help you find your way in the world. Home to Australia’s most employable graduates Bond’s personalised career support is one of the reasons our graduates have been ranked number one in Australia for employer satisfaction, according to the Australian Government’s Employer Satisfaction Survey. We’re also rated five stars for employability in the recent QS Stars ratings. Explore ratings and rankings Career ready Core Curriculum Career development support Transformation programs Student industry experiences Transformer Toggle menu Demo Day at Bond University Startup Bootcamp Transformer Executive Masterclasses Career Development Centre 1:01 play, Explore the Career Development Centre (CDC) in just 61 seconds. Explore the Career Development Centre (CDC) in just 61 seconds. Your career starts here Career planning Career planning A great career starts with a great plan. Our career development specialists in the Career Development Centre can help you identify your interests and discover what really matters to you. How do you want to make a difference in the world? What innate strengths and skills do you have? How do we match those with the right majors and specialisations? Real-life experiences Real-life experiences Throughout your studies, you’ll have the opportunity to gain real-life experience in your chosen area – or areas – of interest through internships, clinical rotations, capstone projects and work placements coordinated by the Career Development Centre, Faculty advisers and lecturers. Network building Network building We’ll put you in the room with potential employers and recruitment specialists through our annual Careers Fair, regular networking events in your chosen industry, mentoring, on-campus guest lectures, study tours and more. Hands-on assistance Hands-on assistance As you approach graduation, we’ll help you polish your application, resume and interview skills in one-on-one career advisory sessions, group workshops and through our exclusive web portal. 1 of 4 Bond students have lifetime access to career development services through the Career Development Centre. Inside the Career Development Centre Your one-on-one career consultants Staffed by a dedicated team of career experts, the goal of the Career Development Centre (CDC) is not just to help find jobs for our graduates but to ensure that Bond students enter the workforce with the skills, experience and confidence to stand out to future employers. The CDC team will work with you one-on-one, in group settings and online, helping you develop job applications and resumes, prepare for interviews and make connections with key employers. They will support you in organising industry placements, internships and even part-time jobs. They also host more than 50 employer events on campus each year, including workshops, seminars, networking events and our annual job and internship fair. As a Bond alum, you will have lifetime access to the CDC team as your personal recruitment advisors. A connected community Create a valuable network from day one Thanks to their industry experience, all of our academics have an extensive network of contacts in their relevant field. Those connections go even further through each Faculty’s established long-term partnerships with key industry players – from international hotel chains and development companies to Australia’s leading law firms, accounting practices, hospitals, healthcare clinics, sporting teams and more. In classes, you will benefit from your academics’ industry contacts and partnerships to open doors to work experience and internship opportunities, and work on projects directly tied to industry. You’ll also have plenty of opportunities to meet with future employers through introductions at on-campus events, guest lectures, industry conferences and inter-university competitions. play, Behind the scenes of Rachael's internship experience Behind the scenes of Rachael's internship experience As the Official Higher Education Partner of World Surf League Australia, Bond students like Rachael Tilly have access to internship opportunities across all facets of the organisation, including sport Management, sports science, event management, marketing and film and television. Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072 This website uses cookies and other tracking technologies to enhance user experience and to analyse performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Manage preferences Reject all Accept cookies Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Data When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalised web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms.  You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work, including our live chat function. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Share Or Sale of Personal Data Share Or Sale of Personal Data Under the CPRA, you have the right to opt-out of the sale "
    },
