rt Medical and health services Student counselling Accessibility and inclusion Accessibility resources Feedback and questions University security Escape | Hide | Tell Emergency contacts Career Development Centre About the Career Development Centre Careers information for all our current students Employers and Industry Global experiences Graduates and alumni Verification of qualifications What's On Preventing and responding to gender-based violence Wellbeing services Student Wellbeing Advisors JP/Commissioner for Declarations service LGBTIQ+ services and support Campus life Bond University Student Association Student clubs Faculty Student Associations Bond University Business Students' Association Health and Sport Sciences Student Association (HSA) Medical Students Society of Bond University (MSSBU) Law Student Association Society & Design Student Association Club events Student events Students living on campus Sports Centre Smoke-free campus Merchandise Store Student Services and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Application procedure Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Study Why study at Bond Career ready Student industry experiences Start of main\n      content. Student industry experiences Bond graduates are the first choice for many leading blue-chip employers, and have been for decades now. Over the years, we have established partnerships with employers that extend beyond the recruitment process, and that have ultimately become an integral part of our award-winning student experience. We have partnerships with industry leaders from all across Australia and the world. You’ll meet representatives from these partnerships from your earliest days at university – at on-campus guest lectures, working on real-life project-based assignments, and at networking events. They are involved in research projects, scholarship programs, and sponsorship of on-campus events, and offer work placement opportunities that can – and have – turned into full-time jobs after graduation. Our industry partners are also integral to our learning experience, serving on advisory boards to ensure our degrees incorporate the most current industry practice. This means that as a Bond student, you’ll be learning the skills and knowledge that are most relevant to your industry of choice and will help you to stand head and shoulders above the rest when you enter the workforce. Career ready Core Curriculum Career development support Transformation programs Student industry experiences Transformer Toggle menu Demo Day at Bond University Startup Bootcamp Transformer Executive Masterclasses Bond degrees are inextricably linked to industry, informed by current practice and standards. Degrees designed by industry – for industry Each of our faculties and study areas are guided by a relevant advisory board, made up of representatives from a broad cross-section of high-profile industry partners. These relationships ensure that our teaching not just meets, but exceeds industry best practice, and is totally up to date with the latest technologies, theoretical underpinnings, processes, and guidelines. One of the benefits of being a small university is that we can quickly respond to new developments and disruptions. The expertise of our advisory boards is what has helped us to get ahead of the curve in creating future-focused learning experiences, such as big data integration and our cutting-edge Transformation degrees . Blurring the line between industry and academia Guest lecturers are a highlight of the Bond learning experience. We have regular events like the Architecture Lecture Series, which features renowned designers from around the world, and Bond Law’s Twilight Seminar Series, which consists of both live panel discussions and webinars. Of course, events just make up one part of our strong involvement with industry in this space – we also welcome industry professionals to guest lecture on campus, providing students with unmatched insight into their career of choice, and offer mentorship from business leaders as part of Transformer , our Australian-first start-up incubator program. Our academics move just as easily between two worlds – consulting to industry, running their own businesses, working in medical, legal, accounting, financial planning practices, conducting research, and presenting at industry conferences, in addition to their roles at Bond. play, Dive into Harrison’s internship with the World Surf League Dive into Harrison’s internship with the World Surf League Only-at-Bond industry experiences Our partnerships with industry lead to exceptional work placements and internships for our students. Travel to a remote Pacific Island to undertake a clinical rotation in a one-doctor hospital, or pursue your love of surf and sand while learning key professional skills with the World Surf League right here on the Gold Coast. Only-at-Bond experiences like these ensure our graduates stand out from the crowd throughout their degrees, and when it’s time to enter the workforce. Unlike at many other universities, these experiences aren’t far and few between, either – our small student cohort means that every student has access to these incredible opportunities. Keep exploring Bond and Chiefs Esports Club announce education alliance Read more Read more about Bond and Chiefs Esports Club announce education alliance Transformer appoints leading entrepreneur Stuart Giles as inaugural Founder in Residence Bond University has recruited one of Australia’s most successful entrepreneurs to help its students forge their own path to business success. Read more Read more about Transformer appoints leading entrepreneur Stuart Giles as inaugural Founder in Residence Bond teams up with Solomon Islands ahead of 2023 Pacific Games Read more Read more about Bond teams up with Solomon Islands ahead of 2023 Pacific Games Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. 