alth services Student counselling Accessibility and inclusion Accessibility resources Feedback and questions University security Escape | Hide | Tell Emergency contacts Career Development Centre About the Career Development Centre Careers information for all our current students Employers and Industry Global experiences Graduates and alumni Verification of qualifications What's On Preventing and responding to gender-based violence Wellbeing services Student Wellbeing Advisors JP/Commissioner for Declarations service LGBTIQ+ services and support Campus life Bond University Student Association Student clubs Faculty Student Associations Bond University Business Students' Association Health and Sport Sciences Student Association (HSA) Medical Students Society of Bond University (MSSBU) Law Student Association Society & Design Student Association Club events Student events Students living on campus Sports Centre Smoke-free campus Merchandise Store Student Services and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Application procedure Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Study Why study at Bond Career ready Transformer Start of main\n      content. Transformer Transformer is an Australian-first entrepreneurship program offered as a fee-free, extracurricular option to undergraduate and postgraduate students from all disciplines. Based in a dedicated co-working space, Transformer brings together students from every area within the University to work in multidisciplinary teams, tasked with developing practical solutions to real-world problems. Whether you’ve discovered a problem that needs to be solved, you have a unique product or service to sell, or are just full of big ideas, Transformer could be the place that nurtures your entrepreneurial spirit and teaches you the skills needed to succeed in the oversaturated business landscape. Whatever you’re passionate about, and whatever your dreams are, Transformer is all about seeing opportunity through entrepreneurial application… it could just be the most life-changing experience you have here at Bond. play, Transformer 1:01 Transformer 1:01 Learn all about the Transformer program in just 61 seconds. Transformer Demo Day at Bond University Startup Bootcamp Transformer Executive Masterclasses Toggle menu Growth & Scale Up Masterclass Collaboration. Conversation. Inspiration. Transformer facilitates collaboration across five distinct areas. As part of Transformer, you will: Experience entrepreneurship with a diverse, culturally inclusive team of students from the full spectrum of faculties and study areas. Participate in workshops on topics ranging from interpersonal to technical skills. Transform your idea into reality through either an individual student venture, group project or global competition. Access industry experts, mentors, coaches and a cutting-edge co-working space. Cross-collaborate with all Bond faculties, alumni, industry and the community. Mentoring from the best in the business A key aspect of the Transformer experience is the opportunity to be mentored and inspired by industry leaders, academics, and alumni. As part of the program, you will have access to complimentary masterclasses and showcases that put you in the room with industry professionals, aspiring entrepreneurs and potential investors. You’ll gain insights from some of Australia’s most successful start-ups and venture capitalists, and be motivated by young achievers who started their journey exactly where you are now. Most importantly, you’ll have the opportunity to connect with Bond’s extensive network of corporate, government and community partners who are proactive in supporting our student entrepreneurs. Transformer Startup Program From Idea to Launch This 12-module program equips founders with the core principles of the Lean Startup methodology. From validating ideas and understanding customer needs to building product-market fit and designing a sustainable business model, each module provides practical steps for startup success. Founders will develop a solution, brand, and pitch strategy, culminating in a launch plan ready for early customer acquisition and investor engagement. Introduction Lean Startup Principles Introduction to key Lean Startup principles, setting the stage for how you approach the startup process with validated learning. Module 1: Ideation Turn Ideas into Opportunities Founder-Market fit. Ensure you have relevant skills, contacts, and interests to operate in your chosen market. Module 2: Customers Know Your Customers and Their Problems Customer-Problem fit. Develop a thorough understanding of your customers and the problems they’re experiencing Module 3: Solutions Create Your Solution Problem-Solution fit. Create a value proposition to solve relevant customer jobs and associated pains and gains. Module 4: Customer Pitch Pitch to Customers Pitch your solution to customers, focusing on how your value proposition solves the customer problem. Module 5: Product Build a Great Product Product-Market fit. Build a product that delights your customers and drives strong growth in the market. Module 6: Business model part 1 Business Model - Desirability Design a business model that addresses desirability risk, ensuring you can deliver a product customers want. Module 7: Business model part 2 Business Model - Feasibility Design a business model that addresses feasibility risk, ensuring you have access to the resources required to build your product. Module 8: Business model part 3 Business Model - Viability Design a business model that addresses viability risk, ensuring you earn sufficient profits to sustain or scale your business. Module 9: Growth and metrics Growth Engines & Metrics Determine the best growth engine for your startup and choose the right metrics to track for your startup, focusing on actionable metrics. Module 10: Branding Create Your Brand Create a strong brand name and logo and build emotional connections with your customers. Module 11: Investors pitch Pitch to Investors Pitch your startup to investors to secure funding. To convince investors you need to think like they do. Module 12: Launch Launch Your Startup Introduce your business to the world with a plan for how to get customers in the early days Launchpad Winner of the Launchpad 231 Ag SafeGuard is founded on experience and research, providing practical solutions to issues faced by Australian landowners. Bait SafeGaurd is a safe, efficient and economical solution for feral pest control using poison bait Angus Croser  - Founder of Ag SafeGuard Winner of the Launchpad 243 The ready-to-drink beverage market is evolving, and TQLA is at the forefront of this transformation. Designed for Gen Z, TQLA offers low sugar, low calories, and unique digestive properties. Chloe aims to redefine how people view tequila-elevating it from late-night shots to smooth, enjoyable sessions. TQLA isn't just a drink-it's a revolution in the beverage industry, blending tradition with a modern twist. Chloe Thomas - Founder of TQLA Winner of Launchpad 233 Uvents The problem: University Event Organisation The solution: Uvents. Did you know it takes 8 different apps to organise 1 university event... and still students have no idea what's happening on campus? Uvents functionality provides Duty of Care, Event Awareness and Safety and Increased Event Attendance. Winner of the Launchpad 233 Ozzie Toole - Founder of Uvents Runner up of Launchpad 251 MYO-N - A next generation myoelectric prosthetic hand that uses machine learning and 3D printing to deliver a personalised, affordable, and comfortable solution. Designed for adaptability and comfort, MYO-N features a self-mouldable socket lining and Al-driven functionality tailored to each user. Lauren Hitchman - Founder of MYO-N Winner of Launchpad 232 Bex Yummy Allergy Free Bakes caters to the top 8 food allergens and more in every product. Trusted by the allergy community, serving families nationwide, Beck is working on the mass production of her wildly successful cake mixes that allow people to recreate her confections at home. Rebecca Bennett - Founder of Bex Yummy AF Bakes Winner of Launchpad 222 Maruma-Li Aboriginal Art offers services with the aim of promoting awareness of the Aboriginal culture and art. We celebrate the incredible Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander history, culture, and accomplishments through the artwork, events, and workshops. Imogen Clarence - Founder of Maruma-Li Aboriginal Art Previous Next 1 of 6 Entrepreneurs are made, not born Each day, it becomes increas"
