ical and health services Student counselling Accessibility and inclusion Accessibility resources Feedback and questions University security Escape | Hide | Tell Emergency contacts Career Development Centre About the Career Development Centre Careers information for all our current students Employers and Industry Global experiences Graduates and alumni Verification of qualifications What's On Preventing and responding to gender-based violence Wellbeing services Student Wellbeing Advisors JP/Commissioner for Declarations service LGBTIQ+ services and support Campus life Bond University Student Association Student clubs Faculty Student Associations Bond University Business Students' Association Health and Sport Sciences Student Association (HSA) Medical Students Society of Bond University (MSSBU) Law Student Association Society & Design Student Association Club events Student events Students living on campus Sports Centre Smoke-free campus Merchandise Store Student Services and Amenities Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Application procedure Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Life at Bond Supporting student success Supporting your career Start of main\n      content. Supporting your career Graduate ready to stand out Navigating the ever-changing career landscape can be tricky. The way we manage our careers is shifting. Industries are evolving. The job market is becoming increasingly competitive. What you do at university has never been more important in setting you apart in the workforce. That’s where Bond’s Career Development Centre comes in. As a Bond student, you will have access to an array of services designed to improve your employability and prepare you to excel after graduation. Featuring a dedicated team of career experts, the goal of the Career Development Centre is simple: ensure that Bond students enter the workforce with the skills, experience, and employability to stand out and get started in their careers. The employability equation What sets graduates apart? Bond’s employability and career services span across three key areas, all of which can be tailored to your career goals and ambitions. 1. Career guidance Your time at university goes beyond the classroom. The Career Development Centre’s team of qualified experts provide a full suite of personalised guidance services. We can help you explore and define your career path, develop applications and resumes, prepare for interviews and make connections with key employers. We hold employer events on campus regularly, including workshops, seminars, networking events and an annual Job and Internship Fair to provide further opportunities to grow your network and improve your skills, ensuring you stand out now, and after you graduate. LEARN MORE 2. Industry placements Our career counselling and industry placement teams are your career champions. We’re here to help you secure internships and placements with Bond’s industry partners. We broker these placements to support your career goals and ensure that they are high-quality experiences with the right supervision and support to make the most of an industry experience. Through placements, you can gain valuable experience and career contacts with leading Australian and international employers. We will help you source placement opportunities, guiding you through the application process and supporting you throughout your placement and beyond. LEARN MORE 3.  Beyond Bond Beyond Bond is a practical program housed within the Transformation CoLab. It is designed to ensure you are well placed to achieve your career goals beyond graduation You will have the freedom to design your own Beyond Bond journey throughout your degree. Select from over 220 activities to earn your points and these could include team sport, student associations, internships or relevant work experience. This non-traditional subject also provides you with the support to access extra-curricular industry placements. LEARN MORE Supporting student success Developing your academic skills Supporting your career Supporting mental health Student advocacy support Indigenous student support LGBTIQ support play, The Career Development Centre The Career Development Centre Be one of Australia’s most desirable graduates Your employability journey During your time at Bond, you'll receive employability support and enhancement opportunities through the following experiences: Personalised career support Engagement with Beyond Bond, our professional development and employability program Extracurricular activities like mooting, Model UN and more Part-time employment, volunteering and community engagement Internships and work experience Graduate employment opportunities and beyond! A lifetime of access Once a Bondy, always a Bondy. As a member of our alumni community, you’ll have lifetime access to Career Development Centre services. Be one of Australia’s most desirable graduates Australia’s #1 university for teaching (Australian Financial Review Best Universities Ranking 2025) #1 in Queensland for skills development (2026 Good Universities Guide) One of Australia’s best student-to-teacher ratios. More about career support at Bond How I secured work experience during my undergraduate degree There's more to becoming a well-rounded professional than just studying. Here's what I learned by pursuing work experience during my degree at Bond. Read more Read more about How I secured work experience during my undergraduate degree Career first: top tips for postgraduate students Thinking about changing lanes, changing your job or changing careers entirely? Read more Read more about Career first: top tips for postgraduate students Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072