 Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Application procedure Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Admissions Officer Start of main\n      content. Admissions Officer Full-Time, Fixed Term until 11 June 2027 Reference number: 201397711 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Work alongside passionate professionals who value teamwork and cooperation Experience a dynamic role encompassing a wide range of tasks Contribute to the university's long-term vision and planning Admissions Officer Office of Future Students Full-Time, Fixed Term until 11 June 2027 Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: 36.75 hour standard work week Access to flexible work/work from home arrangements# Up to 18/26 weeks of parental leave# Salary packaging options for FBT and Non-FBT items# 17.5% of base salary leave loading Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Free staff parking Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# Reporting to the Coordinator, Admissions, the Admissions Officer plays a key role in supporting Bond University’s strategic growth and student recruitment objectives through the accurate, timely, and compliant assessment and processing of admission applications for Bond University and Bond University College. This includes applications from domestic and international students for both coursework and Higher Degree Research programs, scholarships, Study Abroad, and Incoming Exchange pathways. The role is responsible for evaluating academic qualifications from a range of global education systems, verifying supporting documentation, maintaining accurate records, and ensuring all admissions decisions align with university policies, procedures, and legislative requirements. About the person The successful candidate will demonstrate: Relevant qualifications and/or experience in a university, admissions, administration, or other policy-driven environment. A strong commitment to customer service, with the ability to build effective relationships and provide accurate, professional advice to a diverse range of stakeholders. Excellent communication, analytical, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, and legislation while managing competing priorities. High attention to detail and strong organisational skills, with the ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a collaborative team. Proficiency in using student administration, admissions, or other large-scale database systems, with the ability to quickly learn and adapt to new technologies. Cultural awareness and an inclusive approach to working with people from diverse backgrounds; experience in university admissions, compliance requirements, Study Abroad and Exchange programs, and systems such as Study Link, Student One, and Microsoft Dynamics 365 will be highly regarded. Salary details The salary for the position commences at $85,707.07 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Krunal Barot, Manager, Admissions, [email protected] , +61 7 5595 4521 Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Monday, 5th October 2026 Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 5th October 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer CRICOS Provider Code 00017B TEQSA Provider ID PRV12072"
