Fee Bond Sports Centre Group exercise classes Personal training Sports Centre memberships Student housing options Student rights and responsibilities Complaints involving the behaviour of others Advocacy and support Appeals Your responsibilities Your rights Student conduct and misconduct Student surveys Graduate Outcomes Survey Student Experience Survey Opportunities Outbound student mobility Partnering with DFAT Exchange at Bond Participating institutions Asia Europe North America Information sessions Exchange blog How to apply Financial information and funding New Colombo Plan Scholarship 2027 Preparing to go Overseas Back at Bond Frequently asked questions Mooting at Bond What is mooting Mooting opportunities Application procedure Mooting accolades Grants and scholarships Elite Athlete Fund Student Hardship Grant Student Opportunity Fund Frequently asked questions FinTech Hub training Bond Legal Clinics Program The Bond Law Clinic Climate Sustainability Clinic Criminal Law Clinic How to apply Internet Law Research Clinic My Community Legal Clinic Beyond Bond Graduation Preparing to graduate Conferral dates Ceremony information Ceremony videos Graduation booklets Graduation documents MyBond Library iLearn Staff iLearn Library Email Staff Intranet Online Service Catalogue Careers at Bond People Connect Alumni About Bond alumni Online Bond community The Arch Industry and partners Global education partners Sponsorship opportunities News and events News Events Contact Getting to Bond University Campus map Parking Close Home Job vacancy Jobs at Bond Handy Person (Assistant Gardener) Start of main\n      content. Handy Person (Assistant Gardener) Full-time, Continuing Appointment Reference number: 201397636 About the position As Australia’s first private, not-for-profit university, Bond University based in Robina on the Gold Coast seeks to be recognised internationally as a leading independent university, imbued with a spirit to innovate, a commitment to influence and a dedication to inspire tomorrow's professionals who share a personalised and transformational student experience. Help maintain one of Australia’s most beautiful university campuses Join a supportive team where your work makes a visible impact Play a key role in maintaining spaces that support campus life Join Australia’s top university for teaching* and enjoy staff benefits including: Free staff car parking Staff wellbeing program Free & Confidential Employee Assistance Program available for all staff Study assistance for staff and dependents# Corporate health and finance discounts Onsite Medical Centre and Counselling Services Onsite Sports Centre including gym, fitness classes and pool# About the Position Join the Facilities Management team at Bond University and play a key role in maintaining the beautiful campus environment that students, staff and visitors enjoy every day. Reporting to the Head of Grounds, this hands-on position offers the opportunity to contribute to the presentation, upkeep and functionality of the University's outdoor spaces while supporting a range of general facilities activities. As a Handy Person (Assistant Gardener), you will undertake a variety of gardening, maintenance, cleaning and labouring duties using both manual and powered tools and equipment. Working with a supportive and collaborative team, you will enjoy a varied workload, the opportunity to develop your skills through ongoing training, and the satisfaction of seeing the direct impact of your work across one of Australia's most distinctive university campuses. Bond University values safety, inclusion and continuous improvement, providing an environment where employees are encouraged to grow, contribute ideas and take pride in delivering high standards of service. About the person We are seeking a reliable and motivated team player who enjoys outdoor work and takes pride in maintaining high-quality environments. The ideal applicant will have the following: Certificate I or II in a relevant field and/or at least 12 months' practical experience in a similar gardening or grounds maintenance role. Experience using gardening, maintenance and general groundskeeping tools and equipment safely and effectively. The ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines. A commitment to quality workmanship and attention to detail. Knowledge of workplace health and safety practices and a proactive approach to maintaining a safe work environment. Previous experience within a tertiary education environment will be highly regarded. Salary details The salary for the position commences at $68,134.92 per annum, plus 12% superannuation. Additional information Position-related enquiries can be directed to Simon Andrews, Head of Grounds, at [email protected] Application and submission details For further details regarding this appointment, please reference the Position Description and Selection Criteria. Click Apply Now and Create New Account to get started. You can: Upload your Resume – your account will be created automatically, or Manually enter your details to set up your account. Please ensure your application includes: A current resume A cover letter addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description above For current Bond University staff, apply directly via People Connect , log in with staff credentials, from the Home dashboard select Careers, select the role and apply. If you require any assistance with your application submission, please visit Applying for jobs at Bond . Applications close: 11:59pm, Tuesday, 13 October 2026. Pre-employment checks: Appointment is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks (including working rights verification, reference checks and a certified copy of your highest qualification). In line with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025, preferred candidates must complete a Gender-Based Violence (GBV) Declaration, and any offer of employment will be conditional upon the University’s review of the declaration. For more information, please visit our website via this link: Applying for Jobs at Bond Conditions of employment are offered under a Bond Workplace Agreement (BWA). Bond University is an equal opportunity employer, and we encourage our students and staff to respect individuality, inclusiveness and diversity. In line with Bond University’s values, people from diverse backgrounds, women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, people who identify as LGBTIQ+, and people with a disability are encouraged to apply for positions at the University . Please advise the Talent Acquisition Team if you require any reasonable accommodations to assist you at anytime during the recruitment process. For more information, visit Supporting diversity at Bond | Bond University | Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia Bond University Privacy Policy # Eligibility criteria or membership fees apply *Australian Financial Review’s Best Universities Ranking 2024 APPLY NOW Applications close: 13th October 2026 Footer navigation Key Information Bond Care Contact us Giving to Bond Careers at Bond Media enquiries Privacy Policy Disclaimer Quick Links Current students Campus map Library Staff Intranet Feedback and complaints Study Apply at Bond Program Finder Our study areas International students Postgraduate degrees Undergraduate degrees Research & Partners Our research Find a Researcher Research centres Research degrees Partner with Bond Alumni In the spirit of reconciliation, Bond University acknowledges the Kombumerri people, the traditional Owners and Custodians of the land on which the university now stands. We pay respect to Elders past, present and emerging. Read more about our acknowledgment of country Facebook LinkedIn Instagram TikTok YouTube Twitter WeChat Weibo Bond University Privacy Policy Disclaimer